{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed as Gerrit change **3124** — `339c0b3af7b`, branched from `ee5253abfd4`.\n\n`make verify` exits **0**: 19854 passed, 88 skipped, 49m27s.\n\nThe first verify run caught a real gap the plan had missed: `tests/unit/workflow/test_contracts.py:221` built the gate step's *failing-case* fixture from `{\"severity\": \"critical\"}` and asserted `verdict == \"fail\"`. With the severity policy retired that verdict is now `pass`, so the test failed (19853 passed, 1 failed). It was the third severity-driven gate fixture in the tree and the only one the plan did not name. Fixed to `{\"priority\": 0.99}`; a tree-wide sweep of every `steps.gate(` call site confirms no fourth. The 715-test workflow package then passed, and the full re-run is the exit-0 above.\n\nFinal AC status:\n- **AC1** — `git grep` for the three retired identifiers across `src tests docs scripts .github` (less the three documented exclusions) prints nothing.\n- **AC2** — `gen_env_registry.py` regenerated; `docs/env-vars.md` loses the `REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH` row, 149 → 148 variables.\n- **AC3** — satisfied in intent, not in letter; see the preceding comment. `--check` exits 0 (`active=650 new=26 increased=0 stale=0`, all 26 `new` pre-existing and marker-admitted); the baseline shrinks by exactly the one retired entry.\n- **AC4** — `gate_ops.py` has no `read-via: subsystem-kill-switch`; both surviving sites (`src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py:31`, `src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py:148`) confirmed untouched by `git diff` against the base.\n- **AC5** — `plan_review_verdict.schema.json` still lists `severity`; the file is byte-identical to base.\n- **AC6** — `make verify` exits 0.\n\nAlso filed `refreshing-cosmic-jaeger` (`dc9b-e792-bad3-4578`), linked `discovered_from` this story: `review_plan_start` de-duped across the `file_impact` widening and replayed the prior run's verdict as a `stale-material` BLOCK with zero findings. `force=True` produced the real PASS against the same tree. Worth fixing because the misleading verdict reads as a plan defect rather than a swallowed start.\n\nAwaiting `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` before closing."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793160963609512462,"uuid":"72e08520-562e-4dd8-ba33-9fd6363a788f"}